# shadcn/ui Styling Patterns

## Component Usage

Use shadcn-nuxt module or shadcn-vue components. Components are copied into your project - customize them directly.

```vue
<!-- ✅ GOOD - Use shadcn components -->
<template>
  <Button @click="handleSubmit">Calculate</Button>
  <Input v-model="date" type="date" />
  <Card>
    <CardHeader>Results</CardHeader>
    <CardContent>{{ results }}</CardContent>
  </Card>
</template>
```

## Tailwind CSS Patterns

- Use utility classes for styling
- Follow shadcn design tokens (spacing, colors, typography)
- Customize theme in `tailwind.config.js` to match shadcn defaults

```vue
<!-- ✅ GOOD - Consistent spacing -->
<div class="space-y-4 p-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Absence Calculator</h2>
</div>

<!-- ❌ BAD - Inconsistent spacing -->
<div style="padding: 20px;">
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px;">Absence Calculator</h2>
</div>
```

## Component Customization

Modify copied shadcn components in `components/ui/`. Don't modify node_modules.

## Design System Consistency

- Use shadcn color palette (slate, gray, etc.)
- Follow shadcn spacing scale (0.5, 1, 2, 4, 6, 8, etc.)
- Use consistent border radius (default: 0.5rem)
- Match shadcn typography scale

## Mobile-First Responsive Design

Start with mobile styles (base), then enhance for larger screens using Tailwind breakpoints.

```vue
<!-- ✅ GOOD - Mobile-first -->
<div class="w-full px-4 py-6 sm:px-6 md:px-8 lg:px-12">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <!-- Mobile: 1 column, Tablet: 2 columns, Desktop: 3 columns -->
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ❌ BAD - Desktop-first -->
<div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-1">
  <!-- Wrong order - should start mobile-first -->
</div>
```

## Touch-Friendly UI

Ensure all interactive elements meet mobile usability standards.

- Minimum touch target size: 44x44px (use `min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px]`)
- Adequate spacing between interactive elements (at least 8px)
- Use full-width buttons on mobile (`w-full sm:w-auto`)
- Optimize form inputs for mobile keyboards (use appropriate `inputmode`)

```vue
<!-- ✅ GOOD - Touch-friendly -->
<Button class="min-h-[44px] w-full sm:w-auto px-6">
  Calculate
</Button>

<!-- ❌ BAD - Too small for touch -->
<Button class="h-8 px-2">Calculate</Button>
```

## Dark Mode

If implementing dark mode, use shadcn's dark mode utilities (`dark:` prefix).
